  "summary": "The RTL implements the zeroize emergency-erase function using a derived signal zeroize_mask = zeroize & ~bus_busy, which is then used inside the always block labeled zeroize_block to select the next value of the key register (key_q_next). Because zeroize_mask is ANDed with the complement of bus_busy, an asserted zeroize is silently suppressed whenever bus_busy is simultaneously high: the zeroize_block's else-if(bus_wr)/else branches then select either bus_data or the register's own current value key_q_r, so key_q_r is loaded with key_q_next on the next clock edge without being cleared, holding stale key material. This directly violates the design_brief.md contract that zeroize must force key_q to 32'b0 on the next clock edge unconditionally. However, a possible reset synchronization issue on rst_n was also observed and is considered the primary concern pending further investigation. Expected correct behavior for the top candidate: rst_n should deassert cleanly without metastability; this can be verified by simulation of inputs/key_loader_ctrl.v.",
